From bba37a77d314a02dce0e4f11fefd325455931a07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Kunzmann <padix.key@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Sep 2025 12:17:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix setup for CCD components with missing coordinates

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/biotite-dev/hydride/commit/bba37a77d314a02dce0e4f11fefd325455931a07]

setup.py compiles hydride's fragment library at build time by calling
biotite.structure.info.residue() on every component of the Chemical
Component Dictionary, skipping the ones it cannot load. The v1.2.3 tag
only skips KeyError, but biotite >= 1.0 raises ValueError for a CCD
component with missing coordinates (residue(allow_missing_coord=False)),
so with the biotite 1.7.1 that build isolation pulls in from
pypi.riseproject.dev the wheel build aborts in setup.py before any
compiler runs. This is not riscv64-specific: any v1.2.3 build against a
current biotite fails the same way.

Upstream fixed it in bba37a7, which is on the v1.2.4 tag; that tag still
declares __version__ = "1.2.3" and was never uploaded to PyPI, so 1.2.3
remains the latest release and this one-line change is carried onto it.

---
 setup.py | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index e854b94..141f6c0 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -148,7 +148,8 @@ if not isfile(fragment_file_path):
                 print(f"Compiling fragment library... ({i}/{len(mol_names)})", end="\r")
             try:
                 mol = info.residue(mol_name)
-            except KeyError:
+            except ValueError:
+                # Molecule has missing coordinates
                 continue
             std_fragment_library.add_molecule(mol)
     print("Compiling fragment library... Done" + " " * 20)
